            <p class="acc__a">VAPT stands for Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing. It combines vulnerability scanning with manual security testing to identify, validate and prioritize security weaknesses across applications, APIs, networks and IT infrastructure.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="acc__item">
            <summary class="acc__q"><span class="acc__title">What does a VAPT service provider do?</span><span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <p class="acc__a">A VAPT service provider assesses your digital assets for security vulnerabilities and validates exploitable weaknesses through controlled penetration testing. At CipherTrivia, we provide technical findings with severity ratings, evidence and remediation recommendations.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="acc__item">
            <summary class="acc__q"><span class="acc__title">Why is VAPT testing important for businesses?</span><span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <p class="acc__a">VAPT testing helps businesses identify security vulnerabilities before attackers can exploit them. It can reduce security risks across web applications, mobile applications, APIs and infrastructure while supporting internal security assessments and compliance requirements.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="acc__item">
            <summary class="acc__q"><span class="acc__title">What types of VAPT services does CipherTrivia provide?</span><span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <p class="acc__a">We provide web application VAPT, mobile application VAPT, API penetration testing, network VAPT and infrastructure security testing. Our assessments can be scoped according to the applications and infrastructure being tested.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="acc__item">
            <summary class="acc__q"><span class="acc__title">How does CipherTrivia perform VAPT testing?</span><span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <p class="acc__a">We follow a structured process that covers scope definition, vulnerability assessment, manual penetration testing, vulnerability validation, risk classification, reporting and retesting. Our approach combines automated security tools with manual testing performed by security professionals.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="acc__item">
            <summary class="acc__q"><span class="acc__title">Does VAPT include manual penetration testing?</span><span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <p class="acc__a">Yes. Our VAPT security services include manual validation and penetration testing to investigate vulnerabilities identified through automated assessment. Manual testing also helps uncover security issues that automated scanners may not detect.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="acc__item">
            <summary class="acc__q"><span class="acc__title">Do you provide a VAPT report?</span><span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <p class="acc__a">Yes. We provide a detailed VAPT security assessment report containing vulnerability descriptions, severity ratings, technical evidence, affected assets and remediation recommendations. Reports can also include relevant OWASP, CWE and CVSS references.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="acc__item">
            <summary class="acc__q"><span class="acc__title">What vulnerabilities can VAPT identify?</span><span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <p class="acc__a">VAPT can identify vulnerabilities such as SQL injection, Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), broken access control, authentication weaknesses, privilege escalation, insecure configurations, sensitive data exposure and API security vulnerabilities.</p>
